#X text 45 88 [playlist~] is a soundfile player with a playlist. The waveform of the loaded file is drawn across the top with a play/pause button on its left \, and the files are listed underneath. Click a row to load that file \, click or drag the waveform to scrub \, and click the button to start or pause., f 80;
#X obj 200 200 else/playlist~;
#X obj 200 401 else/out~;
#X obj 200 153 loadbang;
#X msg 200 178 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac sax.wav, f 50;
#N canvas 864 118 478 694 interface 0;
#X text 40 30 The object is split in two. The upper strip is the transport: the button on the left starts and pauses playback \, and the rest of it is the waveform of the file that is loaded. Clicking or dragging anywhere in the waveform moves the play position \, and a line marks where playback is., f 64;
#X text 40 100 The lower part is the playlist itself \, one row per file \, numbered from 0 Click a row to load it \, which also stops playback and rewinds to the start. Long names are cut off with an ellipsis., f 64;
#X text 40 160 When there are more files than fit \, a scrollbar appears on the right: the arrows step one row \, dragging the bar jumps and dragging the list itself scrolls it., f 64;
#X text 40 215 The object is graph-on-parent at a fixed 300 by 190 pixels. Note that the same clicks that drive the GUI are also what the 'select' \, 'play' and 'pos' messages do \, so you can drive it either way., f 64;
#X obj 82 392 else/playlist~;
#X obj 82 289 loadbang;
#X msg 82 314 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac sax.wav voice.wav baglama.wav didge.flac violin.flac kantele.flac vacuous.flac, f 26;
#X obj 82 592 else/out~;
#X text 299 317 ten files \, so the list scrolls, f 11;
#X connect 4 0 7 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 4 0;
#X restore 451 408 pd interface;
#N canvas 874 190 486 600 example 0;
#X text 52 10 The outlet is a multichannel signal with 16 channels \, so files of up to 16 channels play back as they are. Use [nchs~] to see the count and [else/select~] or [snake~ out] to pick channels out of it., f 64;
#X obj 107 183 else/playlist~;
#X obj 107 128 loadbang;
#X msg 107 153 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac;
#X obj 24 427 else/nchs~;
#X obj 107 448 else/plate.rev~ 50 0.6 0.25 0.8 0.8, f 22;
#X obj 114 498 else/out~;
#X text 172 392 <= fold the 16 channels down to one, f 12;
#X obj 107 393 else/sum~;
#X floatatom 24 458 5 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 52 61 Here the playlist feeds a reverb. The files are found the same way Pd finds any other file \, so these load from ELSE's own folder. Your own files can sit next to the patch., f 64;
